WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.754
Closing deals takes finding deals.

00:00:05.774 --> 00:00:07.543
But most new-logo reps never

00:00:07.563 --> 00:00:09.163
get the first meeting.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.958
Most prospecting emails get ignored,

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.735
because they talk about the product,

00:00:13.755 --> 00:00:15.099
not the buyer.

00:00:15.517 --> 00:00:17.077
Meet Kelsey Dalton.

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:18.327
Over 10 years in

00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:20.398
enterprise technology sales,

00:00:20.418 --> 00:00:22.616
she rose from account executive to leading

00:00:22.636 --> 00:00:25.533
new-logo teams as a Regional Sales Director

00:00:25.553 --> 00:00:27.481
and a Regional Vice President.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.601
Today she's home with her two kids,

00:00:29.621 --> 00:00:31.011
but her passion for helping

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:33.158
sellers grow hasn't changed.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.806
She built a company's first SMB sales team,

00:00:36.826 --> 00:00:38.693
was named Manager of the Year,

00:00:38.713 --> 00:00:40.360
and saw three of her reps reach

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.664
President's Club in a single year,

00:00:42.684 --> 00:00:45.093
with five more promoted to enterprise.

00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:47.321
Now she's turned the system her

00:00:47.341 --> 00:00:49.221
teams used into a playbook:

00:00:49.241 --> 00:00:51.307
The Repeat Success Method.

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.210
Prioritize the accounts that changed.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.110
Find the people who own the money.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.769
Lead with proof from similar customers.

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:00.644
And follow up with persistence,

00:01:00.664 --> 00:01:02.853
bringing something new every time.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.161
At its heart is a three-part first email:

00:01:06.181 --> 00:01:09.274
a real reason, a similar customer's result,

00:01:09.294 --> 00:01:10.426
and a small ask of

00:01:10.446 --> 00:01:12.385
15 to 20 minutes.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.802
An invitation, not a pitch.

00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:17.624
And one rule above all:

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:19.306
never invent a number.

00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:21.188
Inside:

00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:23.773
email templates you adapt to your own wins,

00:01:23.793 --> 00:01:25.808
an editable scoring toolkit,

00:01:25.828 --> 00:01:27.830
AI prompts for every step,

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.088
and a bonus guide for managers.

00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:32.133
Start with the free guide,

00:01:32.153 --> 00:01:34.105
and watch for the full playbook.

00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:35.995
Root and Reinvent.
